1
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:08,591
[knocking on door]

2
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,220
[knocking continues]

3
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:17,308
-[Mickey] Hi. [chuckles]
-[Gus] Hello.

4
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:23,315
How's it goin'?

5
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:24,566
-Good.
-Good.

6
00:00:24,649 --> 00:00:27,360
I was thinking
we should order some food.

7
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:29,071
Yeah, sure. Okay.

8
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:31,614
Yeah. I'm not hungry now,
but I figured I will be soon.

9
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:33,866
Right. Right, right, right.
Oh, yeah, let's, um...

10
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:36,953
Yeah. Hope it's not too lame
to just hang out here.

11
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:39,164
-No, no. It'll be fun.
-Okay, cool.

12
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:40,957
-Okay. Cool, all right.
-Let's order.

13
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:52,469
[chuckles]

14
00:00:54,179 --> 00:00:56,223
-You wanna order pizza?
-No.

15
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:57,890
I have menus.

16
00:00:59,434 --> 00:01:00,768
[Mickey] These are pretty good.

17
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:04,147
I think Silverlake Ramen's
in here somewhere.

18
00:01:04,231 --> 00:01:05,815
-Good.
-Ooh.

19
00:01:07,192 --> 00:01:09,194
[Mickey tutting]

20
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:12,864
Ye old drug box.

21
00:01:12,947 --> 00:01:15,700
Oh. Okay.

22
00:01:15,783 --> 00:01:18,370
-Should we see what's in here?
-Sure.

23
00:01:18,453 --> 00:01:20,663
Yeah, let's check it out.
I'm curious.

24
00:01:20,747 --> 00:01:23,708
-[sighing] Have a look-see.
-Let's see what we got here.

25
00:01:23,791 --> 00:01:27,212
-Ooh. Edible...
-Okay.

26
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:28,838
Um...

27
00:01:28,921 --> 00:01:30,507
-Ecstasy.
-Mmm-hmm.

28
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:32,759
Got some cocaine.

29
00:01:32,842 --> 00:01:34,677
Got a real party in there.

30
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:35,970
Why, you want it?

31
00:01:37,389 --> 00:01:38,390
Are you serious, or...

32
00:01:38,473 --> 00:01:41,434
I mean, not for us to do together,
'cause I have no use for this, but...

33
00:01:41,518 --> 00:01:43,145
Right. Yeah, uh...

34
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:45,688
No, I'm... I'm good.
Thank you.

35
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:48,608
Was that bad for me to say?
You can tell me if it was.

36
00:01:48,691 --> 00:01:51,027
No, no, I was just more surprised
that you...

37
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:53,988
Never mind.
[stammers] I don't know what's, like,

38
00:01:54,071 --> 00:01:56,408
private about your sobriety
and stuff so I'll just...

39
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:57,992
[inhales sharply]
keep out of it.

40
00:01:58,075 --> 00:02:00,620
No, I... I brought it up. So...

41
00:02:01,538 --> 00:02:03,456
It's fair game. Ask away.

42
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:04,999
No, I just...

43
00:02:05,082 --> 00:02:07,877
I figured if you had it around,

44
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:10,463
you'd be tempted to do it or something.

45
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:11,798
I... I don't know.

46
00:02:11,881 --> 00:02:15,343
Yeah, I mean,
I should throw this shit out.

47
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:18,513
That's what they'd tell me in AA.
It's definitely...

48
00:02:18,596 --> 00:02:20,432
dumb of me to keep it around.

49
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:21,808
Mmm-hmm.

50
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:25,603
So, do you think you would, or...

51
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:27,564
not, or...

52
00:02:27,647 --> 00:02:30,066
Uh, it's just...

53
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:33,861
I think somebody would pay me money
for all this stuff.

54
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:34,946
[Gus chuckles]

55
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:42,078
Whatever. Fine. Fuck it.

56
00:02:45,457 --> 00:02:46,499
[clattering]

57
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:49,001
Hmm.

58
00:02:50,378 --> 00:02:51,713
All right, there's more.

59
00:02:51,796 --> 00:02:53,756
There's more, okay. All right.

60
00:02:55,091 --> 00:02:57,093
Just gonna throw out all the fun ones.

61
00:02:57,969 --> 00:03:00,888
Got this beauty
from a guy in Venice.

62
00:03:00,972 --> 00:03:03,558
-He makes them with his wife and kids.
-Aw...

63
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:08,813
There's something really charming about,
like, a family business, you know?

64
00:03:08,896 --> 00:03:11,899
There should be a Ziploc bag
full of mushrooms in the freezer.

65
00:03:11,983 --> 00:03:13,651
-[objects clattering]
-Oh. Okay.

66
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:15,237
-Did you find it?
-Yeah.

67
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:16,488
-[inhales through teeth]
-Ooh.

68
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:19,198
These are some special mushrooms.

69
00:03:19,282 --> 00:03:22,452
I had one of the best days of my life
tripping on these bad boys at Legoland.

70
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:25,330
One of my best days was at Legoland
and I wasn't even high.

71
00:03:26,831 --> 00:03:30,502
Feels like such a shame to throw 'em out.
Are you sure you don't want 'em?

72
00:03:30,585 --> 00:03:32,629
Nah. I'm not really a shrooms guy.

73
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:35,965
-Have you ever done shrooms?
-No.

74
00:03:37,049 --> 00:03:39,176
-I know that's lame, but--
-It's not lame.

75
00:03:39,261 --> 00:03:41,178
-I don't care.
-I mean, I almost did them.

76
00:03:41,263 --> 00:03:43,640
My buddies and I were gonna do 'em
on a camping trip,

77
00:03:43,723 --> 00:03:45,099
but then we got rained out...

78
00:03:45,182 --> 00:03:48,353
But I feel like since I'd made
the choice to do them...

79
00:03:48,436 --> 00:03:50,355
-Mmm-mmm.
-[Bertie] Hello?

80
00:03:51,188 --> 00:03:52,232
Ah!

81
00:03:52,315 --> 00:03:54,276
-Hello, hello.
-[both] Hey.

82
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:56,236
Uh, where's Randy at?

83
00:03:56,319 --> 00:03:58,029
-I don't know, his house?
-He's not here?

84
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:01,741
-Randy!
-Maybe he was here earlier, but--

85
00:04:01,824 --> 00:04:03,910
-Randy!
-Yeah, I don't think he's here.

86
00:04:03,993 --> 00:04:04,994
Randy!

87
00:04:05,077 --> 00:04:06,454
[door opens]

88
00:04:07,622 --> 00:04:08,623
Hey.

89
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:11,709
Hey, what's up? [exhales]

90
00:04:11,793 --> 00:04:15,129
Randy, I told you if Mickey comes home,
you have to tell her that you're here.

91
00:04:15,212 --> 00:04:16,756
Sorry, I... I didn't want to bother her.

92
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:19,592
I was just in the back
reading a book about dinosaurs.

93
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:22,095
Yeah, it's cool. Just a heads-up
next time would be nice.

94
00:04:22,178 --> 00:04:23,220
[Randy] For sure. Yeah.

95
00:04:23,305 --> 00:04:25,181
Man, I love your guys' place.

96
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:27,392
It's, like, 100 times nicer than my place.

97
00:04:27,475 --> 00:04:30,144
My place is dank and dirty
and gross. [chuckles]

98
00:04:30,227 --> 00:04:32,689
You guys have towels
and toothpaste...

99
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:34,607
So what are you guys up to tonight?

100
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:36,401
I don't know. We're just gonna kick back.

101
00:04:36,484 --> 00:04:39,028
Maybe order some food,
watch a movie...

102
00:04:39,111 --> 00:04:40,947
Kind of a low key thing.

103
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:43,366
I was in the middle of throwing out
some old shrooms.

104
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:45,284
Ooh, really?

105
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:46,911
Just gonna throw 'em out? [chuckles]

106
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:49,831
-Do you want 'em?
-Yes, please.

107
00:04:49,914 --> 00:04:51,374
I didn't know you were into shrooms.

108
00:04:51,458 --> 00:04:53,460
Oh, well, a few years ago,
I spent a whole summer

109
00:04:53,543 --> 00:04:56,338
taking peyote with some skaters
and it changed my life.

110
00:04:56,421 --> 00:04:57,547
I want that summer.

111
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:59,424
Last time I did shrooms
I had a bad trip

112
00:04:59,507 --> 00:05:01,217
and I haven't touched 'em since.
[chuckles]

113
00:05:01,301 --> 00:05:03,594
-Oh, you swore them off?
-Oh, no way.

114
00:05:03,678 --> 00:05:05,930
I've just been waiting for an opportunity
to do it right.

115
00:05:06,013 --> 00:05:08,433
-I can't wait to take back the shrooms.
-This is perfect.

116
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:09,976
You three should do shrooms tonight.

117
00:05:10,059 --> 00:05:12,812
Ooh, yes, very cool.

118
00:05:12,895 --> 00:05:14,356
Yeah, I got no plans.
Let's do it.

119
00:05:14,439 --> 00:05:15,898
-Oh, I don't know.
-[Randy] Yeah.

120
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:17,984
-[Bertie] Cool.
-[Randy] Yeah, that would be fun.

121
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:19,402
Okay, cool.

122
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:20,987
-[Mickey] Yeah.
-Very cool. Yeah.

123
00:05:21,070 --> 00:05:23,865
And I can be, like, the sober guide.
Your guru.

124
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:27,076
I'll set it all up. Make sure you guys
have an excellent trip.

125
00:05:27,159 --> 00:05:30,079
Fantastic. Well, I'm gonna go
get my work clothes off,

126
00:05:30,163 --> 00:05:33,291
-and then we'll get to the magic.
-I am gonna take a bath.

127
00:05:36,085 --> 00:05:37,379
-What?
-What?

128
00:05:37,462 --> 00:05:39,839
-Are you sure you're okay with this?
-Yeah.

129
00:05:39,922 --> 00:05:40,965
This is gonna be fun.

130
00:05:41,048 --> 00:05:43,259
Yes. Should be fun.

131
00:05:43,342 --> 00:05:44,511
Are you scared?

132
00:05:44,594 --> 00:05:45,928
I'm a little scared.

133
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:48,222
It's totally normal
before your first trip.

134
00:05:48,305 --> 00:05:50,558
Are you thinking, like,
"What if it's a bad trip

135
00:05:50,642 --> 00:05:52,769
and it breaks my brain
and I'm never the same?"

136
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:57,106
I wasn't thinking that... no,

137
00:05:57,189 --> 00:05:59,859
but I'll gladly throw that onto the pile.

138
00:05:59,942 --> 00:06:02,361
Uh, no, I guess...

139
00:06:02,445 --> 00:06:03,780
Honestly, I just...

140
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:06,073
I feel a little weird

141
00:06:06,157 --> 00:06:08,117
doing drugs in front of you
when you're sober.

142
00:06:08,201 --> 00:06:09,327
It doesn't feel right.

143
00:06:11,538 --> 00:06:12,914
That's so sweet, but,

144
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:15,249
I never really had an issue with shrooms,
you know?

145
00:06:15,332 --> 00:06:17,419
-It's not like a real trigger for me.
-Mmm-hmm.

146
00:06:17,502 --> 00:06:19,587
And I think everybody should
try them once.

147
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:20,797
They're incredible.

148
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:23,257
Like, I don't fully trust someone
who's never tripped.

149
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:26,761
It's like trusting someone
who still has a Hotmail account.

150
00:06:26,844 --> 00:06:30,056
Oh, yeah. It's like when you meet somebody
who hasn't seen Die Hard.

151
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:32,391
And you're like... "Who are you?"

152
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:35,853
-Yeah, everybody's seen Die Hard.
-You haven't seen Die Hard?

153
00:06:36,854 --> 00:06:38,856
[theme music playing]

154
00:06:55,498 --> 00:06:56,958
[Randy] The stems make you trip longer,

155
00:06:57,041 --> 00:07:00,002
but the caps will give you,
like, a deeper trip.

156
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:01,838
-Is that true?
-Yeah.

157
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:05,299
And, the thing is, they taste like shit,
but that's great.

158
00:07:05,382 --> 00:07:07,802
They're supposed to.
If it tastes like shit, it's a good thing.

159
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:10,638
No, there's no reason
why they have to taste like shit.

160
00:07:10,722 --> 00:07:14,559
Take a sandwich.
See, you eat this, it masks the taste

161
00:07:14,642 --> 00:07:18,521
and it provides a good basis
in your stomach for digestion.

162
00:07:18,605 --> 00:07:20,940
-[Gus] Ah, okay. Genius.
-Mmm-hmm.

163
00:07:21,023 --> 00:07:22,900
That's good. Smart.

164
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:24,944
All right. Down the hatch.

165
00:07:26,028 --> 00:07:27,154
[Mickey claps]

166
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:33,578
[sighs]

167
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:39,626
Mmm.

168
00:07:39,709 --> 00:07:42,504
So, like, how long does it typically
take to kick in?

169
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:44,005
-Ten minutes.
-Like, an hour.

170
00:07:44,088 --> 00:07:45,214
Oh. [chuckles]

171
00:07:45,297 --> 00:07:47,216
Getting conflicting reports there.

172
00:07:47,299 --> 00:07:48,384
Oh, that's normal.

173
00:07:48,467 --> 00:07:50,887
It hits some people quicker than others.
It's all good.

174
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:56,392
This actually is a really good sandwich.

175
00:07:58,477 --> 00:08:00,772
[mellow music playing]

176
00:08:03,691 --> 00:08:06,068
That's pretty much what you can do
with those things.

177
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:07,361
[game rattles]

178
00:08:10,406 --> 00:08:12,617
I feel like I don't feel anything.

179
00:08:13,701 --> 00:08:16,829
But if you guys said you were
feeling something then,

180
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:18,915
then I'm probably
feeling it, too.

181
00:08:20,457 --> 00:08:21,668
-I don't feel anything.
-Nah.

182
00:08:22,544 --> 00:08:24,045
What if we dance? Huh?

183
00:08:24,128 --> 00:08:26,088
-That's a good trick.
-Okay.

184
00:08:27,715 --> 00:08:28,883
[pop music playing]

185
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:30,802
Get your asses up. Come on.

186
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:34,388
You gotta do it big
and loud and stupid!

187
00:08:35,306 --> 00:08:37,559
-Bertie?
-Okay, yes.

188
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:43,940
It gets that mushroom blood
straight to the brain.

189
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:45,733
I'm gonna kill you
if you don't get up now.

190
00:08:45,817 --> 00:08:47,109
[Bertie] Come on, Randy.

191
00:08:48,069 --> 00:08:50,487
Move it. Groove it.

192
00:08:50,572 --> 00:08:51,823
More!

193
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:54,158
Use your whole body.

194
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:21,102
[Gus breathing heavily]

195
00:09:27,859 --> 00:09:29,110
How you doing there, bud?

196
00:09:29,736 --> 00:09:31,070
I'm good.

197
00:09:32,864 --> 00:09:35,324
[breathing heavily]
Are they kicking in?

198
00:09:35,407 --> 00:09:38,620
Can't say for sure, but it seems like
they might be kickin' in.

199
00:09:38,703 --> 00:09:40,287
Okay. This is gonna be fun.

200
00:09:41,205 --> 00:09:43,082
Yeah. [exhales deeply]

201
00:09:44,541 --> 00:09:45,668
Are they kickin' in?

202
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:49,756
Hey... [grunts]

203
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:52,800
[sighs]

204
00:09:52,884 --> 00:09:54,886
We're free to share
bad thoughts here, right?

205
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:57,597
I don't want to ruin your trip,

206
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,641
but I feel like if I, like,

207
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:02,393
keep bad stuff in my head
and don't share it,

208
00:10:02,476 --> 00:10:03,728
then I'm gonna have a bad trip.

209
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:06,438
-You know what I mean? Like...
-Totally.

210
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:08,024
It's just like... [sighs]

211
00:10:09,066 --> 00:10:11,027
I look at this house
and I'm like...

212
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:15,281
"Will I ever own a home like this?

213
00:10:15,364 --> 00:10:18,492
Or, am I just gonna be somebody
who lives in some...

214
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:23,289
sad apartment his entire life
and then dies?"

215
00:10:24,081 --> 00:10:25,625
Yep.

216
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:28,878
I live at the Springwood,
so that's like my entire existence.

217
00:10:28,961 --> 00:10:30,462
If I was gonna do something
significant with my life,

218
00:10:30,546 --> 00:10:32,339
it already would've happened by now.

219
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:35,217
Right now, in our lives,
we're at that part, in a movie,

220
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:38,429
when something cool
should start happening, but it's not.

221
00:10:39,346 --> 00:10:41,974
We're over a half an hour
into Jurassic Park...

222
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:44,727
and the dinosaurs haven't even shown up.

223
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:47,689
They're never gonna fuckin' show up.

224
00:10:48,272 --> 00:10:49,606
This candle...

225
00:10:51,275 --> 00:10:53,361
I look at this candle and I think...

226
00:10:54,278 --> 00:10:56,864
we all just want to be warm,
you know?

227
00:10:56,948 --> 00:10:59,408
Everyone on this planet...

228
00:10:59,491 --> 00:11:02,494
we're all just seeking warmth.
That's all we want.

229
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:05,289
That's true. That's very cool.

230
00:11:06,832 --> 00:11:09,960
I don't wanna forget that I said that,
so can you write that down, please?

231
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:12,505
My brain's not friends
with my hands right now.

232
00:11:12,922 --> 00:11:14,506
[both laugh]

233
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:24,016
You wanna go outside? That usually
feels good when you're tripping.

234
00:11:25,017 --> 00:11:26,936
I trust you entirely at this point.

235
00:11:31,315 --> 00:11:32,316
[door opens]

236
00:11:37,321 --> 00:11:39,782
[Randy] Gus, this is a child's toy,

237
00:11:39,866 --> 00:11:41,617
but it is the tool of a man.

238
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,285
[Randy and Gus laugh]

239
00:11:44,203 --> 00:11:46,455
Do you wanna hear
my American accent?

240
00:11:46,538 --> 00:11:47,664
Yeah.

241
00:11:47,749 --> 00:11:49,416
[American accent]
"I think Trask Industries

242
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:51,168
should invest in the radio market."

243
00:11:51,252 --> 00:11:52,754
-Is that from Working Girl?
-[normal] Yes.

244
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:55,339
-I'm a huge fan.
-Oh, me too.

245
00:11:55,422 --> 00:11:59,301
I love Working Girl so fucking much.

246
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:02,096
[Bertie] Yeah. Han Solo looks great
in a suit.

247
00:12:02,179 --> 00:12:06,267
Even after all these years,
human beings are still the same.

248
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:11,397
Everybody talks about evolution,
but nobody talks about how long it takes.

249
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:13,565
We're still not evolved.

250
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:15,067
Really? You think?

251
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:17,361
We have the brains of barbarians

252
00:12:17,444 --> 00:12:18,737
even though we don't live

253
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:20,114
-in caves anymore.
-Mmm-hmm.

254
00:12:20,197 --> 00:12:25,077
We've, like, evolved properly
for hunting, for killing,

255
00:12:25,161 --> 00:12:27,121
and for sucking the blood
from animals.

256
00:12:27,204 --> 00:12:29,415
-Literally!
-Yes, I... I get it.

257
00:12:29,498 --> 00:12:31,125
-I get it, yeah. I get your point.
-Yes.

258
00:12:31,208 --> 00:12:33,627
I... Not... [stuttering]

259
00:12:33,710 --> 00:12:36,547
I'm not gonna kill you,
but if I want to kill you,

260
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:37,882
I could...

261
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:41,593
I could put my thumbs
through your eyeballs, like that,

262
00:12:41,677 --> 00:12:44,305
-and you'd be dead in a second.
-What?

263
00:12:44,388 --> 00:12:47,766
You know, Bertie, I feel like,
whether it's, like, tonight...

264
00:12:48,893 --> 00:12:51,728
or way, way, way, way in the future,
like, you and me...

265
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:54,816
-we're gonna be friends forever.
-Definitely.

266
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:56,358
I knew that when we first met,

267
00:12:56,442 --> 00:12:59,987
when we were just two crazy kids
carrying furniture.

268
00:13:00,071 --> 00:13:01,655
Right. On the lawn there.

269
00:13:01,738 --> 00:13:03,324
We... we were carrying in...

270
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:05,701
your thing.

271
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:07,161
-My dresser?
-Your dresser.

272
00:13:07,244 --> 00:13:10,706
Yeah. Oh, my God. That feels
like it was, like, a month ago.

273
00:13:10,789 --> 00:13:12,875
Well, it was like, three weeks ago. Yeah.

274
00:13:14,335 --> 00:13:16,753
We should move something again.
That felt good.

275
00:13:18,422 --> 00:13:23,010
I could take both of my hands
and smoosh your head...

276
00:13:23,094 --> 00:13:25,096
like a watermelon, right now.

277
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:27,764
'Cause that is something
that's in my blood.

278
00:13:27,849 --> 00:13:29,516
I'm part barbarian,
you know what I mean?

279
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:31,978
You... What are you doing?

280
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:33,270
-Oh, my God.
-If I wanted to,

281
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:36,023
I could put you in a bag
and hit you against a tree.

282
00:13:36,107 --> 00:13:38,525
I get it! You're big and you're strong.
'Kay, guys,

283
00:13:38,609 --> 00:13:40,903
can you please not do that
right now? Please?

284
00:13:40,987 --> 00:13:42,864
-It feels right.
-[Mickey] Well, it's official.

285
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:44,406
You're all peaking.

286
00:13:45,407 --> 00:13:47,409
Excuse me. [sighs]
I gotta take care of something.

287
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:50,662
The cavemen weren't even
that different from us.

288
00:13:50,746 --> 00:13:54,333
They grew hair on their face
just like I have on my face.

289
00:13:55,251 --> 00:13:57,711
[Gus and Bertie whooping and laughing]

290
00:14:00,214 --> 00:14:01,883
-[Randy laughing]
-[door opening]

291
00:14:02,841 --> 00:14:04,635
-Hey. Hey.
-Hey.

292
00:14:05,761 --> 00:14:06,762
[sighs]

293
00:14:06,845 --> 00:14:09,556
Seems like you guys
are havin' some fun out there.

294
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:10,766
Mmm-hmm.

295
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:12,894
-Maybe I should come join you.
-Yeah!

296
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:15,938
You want to? I was just comin' in
to see if you wanna...

297
00:14:16,022 --> 00:14:17,398
pop on out where we're havin' fun.

298
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:20,359
Maybe I'll take this little guy.

299
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:23,695
-You think that's a good idea?
-They're not addictive.

300
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:25,907
They're not really even a drug.

301
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:27,616
Right. [sighs]

302
00:14:27,699 --> 00:14:31,954
Right, I just feel like it's not a...
good idea, 'cause, um...

303
00:14:35,416 --> 00:14:37,376
Sorry, it's really hard
to form an argument

304
00:14:37,459 --> 00:14:39,336
when I'm, like,
watching the bedspread swirl.

305
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:40,629
-Um...
-You know what?

306
00:14:40,712 --> 00:14:43,090
Don't worry about it.
It's fine.

307
00:14:43,174 --> 00:14:45,885
No. Mickey, don't do it.

308
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:47,929
-I just--
-Okay?

309
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:50,306
-Oh, I really want to.
-No. Mickey, don't.

310
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:51,807
It'll be fine. Calm down.

311
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:53,184
-Don't do it. Don't.
-[grunts]

312
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:56,270
-Don't, don't, don't.
-Fuck! Gus, what the fuck?

313
00:14:56,353 --> 00:14:58,230
[gulps and gasps] I'm sorry.

314
00:14:58,981 --> 00:15:00,733
I'm sorry. I just didn't want you to...

315
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:02,651
Uh, fuck!

316
00:15:03,235 --> 00:15:04,570
Mickey, why did I do that?

317
00:15:04,653 --> 00:15:06,863
-Am I gonna be okay?
-Yeah.

318
00:15:06,948 --> 00:15:10,034
-Am I gonna die?
-No! You took a small dose to begin with.

319
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:12,203
You're...
probably just gonna have more fun.

320
00:15:12,286 --> 00:15:14,246
[chuckles] Okay.

321
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:18,375
Come here. Come here.

322
00:15:19,543 --> 00:15:20,836
[sighs] Oh, God.

323
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,838
This tastes, like, so bad.

324
00:15:22,921 --> 00:15:25,632
I, like, totally get why you put it
in a peanut butter sandwich.

325
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:27,801
[Randy] Holy fuck. Gus?

326
00:15:27,884 --> 00:15:29,053
Fuck's goin' on out there?

327
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:32,014
-I don't know.
-There's a creature in the backyard here.

328
00:15:32,098 --> 00:15:34,433
There's a beast in the backyard!

329
00:15:34,516 --> 00:15:35,977
Gus.

330
00:15:37,269 --> 00:15:40,356
Oh, shit. That's a coyote.

331
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:44,276
[chuckles] That is... one handsome animal.

332
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:46,362
Dude, don't go near him.
He can hurt you.

333
00:15:46,445 --> 00:15:47,529
His coat.

334
00:15:48,113 --> 00:15:49,657
He's so majestic.

335
00:15:50,532 --> 00:15:51,908
[breathing heavily]

336
00:15:51,993 --> 00:15:53,744
[clicking tongue]

337
00:15:55,246 --> 00:15:56,247
Coyote.

338
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:59,125
[Mickey] Hey, that's a wild animal.
How about we leave him alone?

339
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:02,128
Definitely back off, 'cause its, like,
teeth could rip at your flesh.

340
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:05,589
Oh, no, no.
He's one of the good ones.

341
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:07,758
Aren't you, buddy?

342
00:16:07,841 --> 00:16:10,886
You and I aren't that different.
We're both... beasts.

343
00:16:10,969 --> 00:16:12,888
-[whines softly]
-But you are covered in fur.

344
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:14,723
And I am in flesh.

345
00:16:14,806 --> 00:16:16,475
Neither of you have jobs.

346
00:16:16,558 --> 00:16:19,145
Coyote. Coyote.

347
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:21,272
Randy. Coyote.

348
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:23,524
Randy. Coyote.

349
00:16:23,607 --> 00:16:26,110
-Okay, enough with that.
-I can feel his essence.

350
00:16:26,193 --> 00:16:29,113
He's here for a reason.
Don't you guys feel that?

351
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:31,532
-No... not really.
-[Bertie and Gus] No.

352
00:16:31,615 --> 00:16:33,534
-Hey, let's go back inside.
-[clicking tongue]

353
00:16:33,617 --> 00:16:36,954
-[Gus] Yeah, Randy, I...
-[Randy] Oh, no. No.

354
00:16:37,038 --> 00:16:39,498
-No, Randy. Stop. Oh, shit.
-[Gus] Randy! Randy!

355
00:16:39,581 --> 00:16:41,166
-[Mickey] Dude, come on!
-[Gus] No!

356
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,793
[Gus] They don't like to be chased.

357
00:16:42,876 --> 00:16:45,045
-[Mickey] Randy, stop. Shit.
-[Randy] No. No.

358
00:16:52,886 --> 00:16:55,139
-[Mickey] Fuck! Shit.
-[Bertie] Randy.

359
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:56,973
[Mickey] Randy, seriously, stop.

360
00:16:57,058 --> 00:16:58,767
Listen to me, I am your guide.

361
00:16:58,850 --> 00:17:01,145
[panting] You're not my guide.

362
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:02,688
This coyote is my guide.

363
00:17:02,771 --> 00:17:05,816
Randy, why don't you choose
another animal to be your guide?

364
00:17:05,899 --> 00:17:08,527
Like a nice bird or a squirrel?

365
00:17:08,610 --> 00:17:11,738
Yeah, I gotta say, shroom buddy,
this isn't the smartest move right now.

366
00:17:11,822 --> 00:17:13,449
I gotta follow him.

367
00:17:13,532 --> 00:17:15,492
My friend. Wait for me.

368
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:18,996
-Ugh. I feel sick runnin' so fast.
-Okay, that's common on shrooms.

369
00:17:19,079 --> 00:17:20,706
Try and keep a low center of gravity.

370
00:17:20,789 --> 00:17:22,374
-Okay.
-Okay?

371
00:17:44,855 --> 00:17:46,273
[Mickey] Randy, come back, dude.

372
00:17:46,357 --> 00:17:49,068
You don't get it.
He'll show me my destiny.

373
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:50,361
Gus knows what I'm talkin' about.

374
00:17:50,444 --> 00:17:53,197
The coyote. My legacy. He knows it.

375
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:54,615
The coyote doesn't know anything.

376
00:17:54,698 --> 00:17:56,242
The Native Americans say
that they're wise.

377
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:59,703
-You disagree with them, Gus?
-Oh, now this is getting scary.

378
00:17:59,786 --> 00:18:01,663
He's really starting to scare me.

379
00:18:01,747 --> 00:18:04,500
[groans] Jesus Christ.
I am the worst drug guide ever.

380
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,263
[chuckles]

381
00:18:17,346 --> 00:18:18,430
[exhales in awe]

382
00:18:18,514 --> 00:18:19,723
Randy?

383
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:25,146
[breathing heavily] This house.

384
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:26,772
This house is beautiful.

385
00:18:26,855 --> 00:18:29,483
This house is the answer the coyote
was leading me to.

386
00:18:29,566 --> 00:18:32,068
[Gus] I don't know, Randy.
This house is pretty basic.

387
00:18:32,153 --> 00:18:33,654
This is my home.

388
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:37,158
Stop, Randy.

389
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:38,909
That's trespassing.

390
00:18:39,618 --> 00:18:40,952
I gotta get in.

391
00:18:41,912 --> 00:18:43,956
[whispers] Randy. Don't, don't, don't.

392
00:18:44,039 --> 00:18:46,375
Come on.
This is starting to feel illegal, man.

393
00:18:46,458 --> 00:18:48,169
There's always more than one opening.

394
00:18:48,252 --> 00:18:50,045
Randy. No, do not go in there. No.

395
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:51,963
Randy, you're acting like a maniac.

396
00:18:52,047 --> 00:18:53,799
[Gus] Randy, don't.

397
00:18:53,882 --> 00:18:55,968
-[Mickey] Don't do that.
-[Bertie] Stop that, please.

398
00:18:56,051 --> 00:18:58,178
-[Gus] Don't do that.
-[Bertie] Put it back on the window.

399
00:18:58,262 --> 00:19:00,472
Randy, listen to me.
Get away from that house.

400
00:19:00,556 --> 00:19:02,683
-[Gus] Randy. Randy, don't.
-[Mickey] Randy, don't. No.

401
00:19:02,766 --> 00:19:05,686
-[Mickey] Please. Please don't do this!
-[Bertie] Randy, no!

402
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:07,646
-[Randy grunts] Ow.
-[Bertie] Randy.

403
00:19:07,729 --> 00:19:09,690
[Randy] Wow.
This guy's got a lot of books.

404
00:19:09,773 --> 00:19:11,400
[sighs] I'm gonna go handle this.

405
00:19:11,483 --> 00:19:13,444
I can do this. I'm not that messed up.

406
00:19:13,527 --> 00:19:15,070
Dude, you are super messed up right now.

407
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:16,905
Your eyeballs are, like,
30 feet wide.

408
00:19:16,988 --> 00:19:18,031
No, they're not.

409
00:19:18,114 --> 00:19:19,783
-I can do this. I...
-[Bertie] Randy.

410
00:19:19,866 --> 00:19:22,869
Don't run away. Help me.
Pull me in. [grunts]

411
00:19:22,953 --> 00:19:25,121
-[sighs]
-Yeah, I got this.

412
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:27,249
-[Bertie] Ow!
-[Gus] Bertie, I'm behind you.

413
00:19:27,333 --> 00:19:29,125
-Keep the window open.
-[sighs] Oh, my God.

414
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:32,838
[whispering] Randy.

415
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:36,383
Randy.

416
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:44,850
[whispering] Randy?

417
00:19:50,814 --> 00:19:52,233
Randy?

418
00:19:56,403 --> 00:19:58,239
I smell him.

419
00:20:05,246 --> 00:20:07,539
-[whispering] Come on, Bertie.
-Oh, did you see this?

420
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:09,791
Yes. It's a stove.

421
00:20:09,875 --> 00:20:12,378
-We have to find Randy.
-Okay.

422
00:20:12,461 --> 00:20:14,963
Randy? Randy?

423
00:20:15,964 --> 00:20:18,759
Jesus Christ, man.
Come on. Dude.

424
00:20:19,676 --> 00:20:21,470
[Randy] Why can't I have a bed like this?

425
00:20:21,553 --> 00:20:23,472
It's firm but soft on top.

426
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:25,015
I love this bed, Gus.

427
00:20:25,098 --> 00:20:26,600
-Okay, all right, Randy.
-Mmm?

428
00:20:26,683 --> 00:20:28,644
Hey, we really shouldn't be here, okay?

429
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:30,937
The coyote helped you out,
and that's awesome...

430
00:20:31,021 --> 00:20:33,524
but we need to get home now.
Okay, buddy?

431
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,942
I don't wanna get home.
I'm very comfortable here.

432
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:38,320
-Everything I need is here.
-I know.

433
00:20:38,403 --> 00:20:40,113
I know, but we should get out of here.

434
00:20:40,196 --> 00:20:41,573
-Okay, let's go.
-Randy, please.

435
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:45,702
-I really don't like what's happening.
-[sighs] Oh, my God.

436
00:20:45,786 --> 00:20:47,913
You are so in your head right now.

437
00:20:47,996 --> 00:20:50,582
What's happening to you
is irrelevant to me.

438
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:52,208
I'm not going anywhere.

439
00:20:52,293 --> 00:20:54,461
This is breaking and entering,
you idiots.

440
00:20:54,545 --> 00:20:56,129
I'm very happy here.

441
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:59,090
-Oh, no.
-Shit.

442
00:20:59,174 --> 00:21:00,342
Oh, great, they're home.

443
00:21:00,426 --> 00:21:01,677
That could be anybody.

444
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,387
Oh, Randy, I'm begging you,
please get up.

445
00:21:03,470 --> 00:21:05,472
You know what? We gotta go.
I'll help you, okay?

446
00:21:05,556 --> 00:21:07,933
-[grunting]
-No. You guys can go.

447
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:09,059
Jesus.

448
00:21:09,142 --> 00:21:11,186
I need to chill here,
and await the next message.

449
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:14,481
-Help me out here, Randy. Come on.
-Just fucking hurry. Enough of this.

450
00:21:14,565 --> 00:21:16,274
Let's get the fucking show on the road.

451
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:18,944
-[Bertie] Oh, God. Oh, God.
-[breathes shakily] Randy?

452
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:21,738
You are being a rude asshole right now.

453
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:23,949
You're on drugs,
and you're gonna fuck up our lives.

454
00:21:24,032 --> 00:21:26,327
So stop being a rude asshole!

455
00:21:27,578 --> 00:21:28,620
Yeah, okay.

456
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:30,706
-Come on. Just leave the blanket.
-[Mickey] Go! Go!

457
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:32,958
You're gonna leave the fucking blanket,
Randy.

458
00:21:33,041 --> 00:21:36,587
[Mickey] Come on, come on, come on.
Okay. Okay, good, good. Oh, shit.

459
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:37,713
Okay, we gotta go.

460
00:21:48,932 --> 00:21:50,266
[laughs]

461
00:21:51,184 --> 00:21:52,227
[Bertie laughs]

462
00:21:53,144 --> 00:21:54,438
[Gus laughs]

463
00:21:57,190 --> 00:21:58,567
[laughter continues]

464
00:22:00,652 --> 00:22:02,654
[Randy] That was fucking crazy.

465
00:22:02,738 --> 00:22:04,197
[Gus continues laughing]

466
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:16,918
Hey, are you still tripping?

467
00:22:17,002 --> 00:22:19,880
Mmm... Not so much.

468
00:22:19,963 --> 00:22:23,299
I mean, I have little pockets
here and there, but...

469
00:22:23,384 --> 00:22:24,551
I think I'm done.

470
00:22:24,635 --> 00:22:26,803
-Mmm.
-Yeah.

471
00:22:26,887 --> 00:22:28,179
[sighs]

472
00:22:28,972 --> 00:22:31,517
I felt, like, I, like,
actually learned, like...

473
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:34,019
like a really good lesson tonight.

474
00:22:34,102 --> 00:22:36,772
-Oh, yeah, what?
-Like...

475
00:22:37,564 --> 00:22:39,608
It's really fun to do drugs?

476
00:22:39,691 --> 00:22:41,568
[chuckles]

477
00:22:41,652 --> 00:22:45,781
Not the most profound takeaway,
but I like the spirit of it.

478
00:22:46,615 --> 00:22:49,117
I don't know, it's cool.
It's like, um...

479
00:22:51,495 --> 00:22:53,163
you pushed me a little
closer to the ledge.

480
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:54,540
Yeah.

481
00:22:54,623 --> 00:22:57,709
And you... you pulled me back from it.

482
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:59,503
[sighs deeply]

483
00:23:02,881 --> 00:23:05,426
Yeah.
I'd say it's a good team, you know?

484
00:23:05,509 --> 00:23:07,719
-Mmm-hmm.
-Fuck! Shit.

485
00:23:07,803 --> 00:23:08,970
Sorry.

486
00:23:09,888 --> 00:23:11,640
-Sorry, Micks.
-It's cool.

487
00:23:12,683 --> 00:23:14,184
[Gus] Oh.

488
00:23:15,811 --> 00:23:19,856
